attorneys.bio:
Ivy League educated attorney with over 37 years of experience, his expertise encompasses estate planning, trusts, wills & probate, and inheritance.

Bilingual and Fluent in Spanish.

He is both a licensed attorney and CPA with a Master of Taxation.

Martinez is a member of The Florida Bar Real Property, Probate & Trust Law Section, and the Elder Law Section.

He is a member of The Florida Bar and the Florida Institute of Certified Public Accountants. He is admitted to practice before the United States Tax Court. He is also a member of the American Academy of Attorney-CPAs.

Martinez earned

his Master’s Degree in Taxation from Florida International University,

his law degree from Columbia University School of Law,

and his undergraduate B.B.A. degree in accounting, Cum Laude, from the University of Miami

where he was a Henry King Stanford Scholar and graduated with a Certificate of Excellence. While attending UM he was a member of the university accounting, business and scholastic honor societies.

He has served the community as:

Miami-Dade Councilman, South Bay 15, Community Council and Zoning Appeals Board;

President of the University of Miami Alumni Club of Greater Miami;

Vice-President of the University of Miami Hurricane Club;

Second Vice Commander, Sons of American Legion, South Miami;

Treasurer, Miami-Dade Agricultural Foundation;

Miami-Dade County South Corridor Citizen's Transportation Advisory Committee;

Vice President, Miami Buena Vista Lions Club;

Elks Lodge, Sunset.

Awards and Honors

Honors

5.0 rating from Martindale-Hubbell

